@startuml request-flowchart
' ============================================================================
'  agentd - Request Flow + DETAILED Agent Loop (one user message, top to bottom).
'  Shows every decision in the reason->act loop, the incomplete-turn handling,
'  tool selection, and the sealed `computer` sub-loop.
'  GOLD steps = PROPOSED (plan-first), not built yet — for review before we add it.
'  Render (from this folder):
'    java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -tpng request-flowchart.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #6A6A6A
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4E5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #C9A227
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam partitionBorderColor #9AA0B5
skinparam partitionFontStyle bold
skinparam partitionFontSize 13

title agentd - Request Flow + Agent Loop (detailed)\nEvery decision in the reason -> act loop.  GOLD = PROPOSED (plan-first), not built yet.

start

partition "1 . CLIENT" #E8F0FE {
  :User sends a message over one WebSocket;
}

partition "2 . GATEWAY  (presentation, localhost)" #FDECEA {
  :reply { runId } immediately, run the agent ASYNC;
  :tag the run with this client (disconnect -> abort);
}

partition "3 . APPLICATION  (AgentService.handle_message)" #E8F5E9 {
  :load session history (JSONL);
  :append the user message;
  :build the system prompt\n(identity . ## Language . tool list + descriptions . ## Skills . safety);
}

partition "4 . AGENT LOOP   (engine: reason -> act, repeats until done / error / max turns)" #EDE7F6 {

  :inject steering messages (optional, before the first turn);

  repeat :begin a turn   (turn_start, message_start);

    :STEP 1 - STREAM THE LLM   (litellm_stream)\nsend: system prompt + FULL history + every tool's SCHEMA & DESCRIPTION\nmodel streams:  (a) thinking  ->  (b) visible text  ->  (c) maybe TOOL CALLS\nguards: idle-timeout 120s + request-timeout  (a hung stream ends gracefully);

    'STEP 1b - PLAN-FIRST (PROPOSED, not built): GATED on complexity, NOT always.
    if (STEP 1b - PROPOSED: is the task COMPLEX / multi-step, and no plan yet?) then (yes - complex)
      #Gold:call the `plan` tool -> numbered steps + WHICH TOOL each needs.\nSaved to history, shown + updated every turn. (It's a TOOL CALL, so the\nloop treats planning as an ACTION, not a "stalling" text turn.);
    else (no - simple / 1-2 steps)
      #Gold:SKIP planning - just act on it directly\n(no plan tool, no overhead);
    endif

    switch (STEP 2 - what did the model produce this turn?)

    case ( it requested TOOL CALLS )
      :the model ALREADY chose each tool\nby matching the task to the tool DESCRIPTIONS\n(better descriptions -> better tool choice);
      partition "5 . TOOLS   (EVERY call wrapped by GuardedTool)" #E1F5FE {
        :validate args vs the tool's JSON schema\n(bad args -> error result, no execution);
        :GuardedTool: per-tool TIMEOUT + RETRY + error-normalize\n(slow / stuck tool -> clean error, the run continues);
        :run the chosen tool ->\nread . write . edit . ls . find . exec . process .\nweb_search . web_fetch . browser . plan(PROPOSED) . computer;
        :append the tool result(s) to history;
      }
      #Gold:(PROPOSED) mark the current plan step done / update the plan;
      ->results feed back to STEP 1;

    case ( a FINAL TEXT answer )
      :classify the turn - is it ACTUALLY complete?\n(engine: classify_incomplete_turn);
      if (planning-only / reasoning-only / EMPTY?) then (INCOMPLETE)
        :emit `continuation`; inject\n"don't just plan - ACT now / produce the answer"\n(capped: a few retries per kind);
      elseif (a follow-up message is queued?) then (yes)
        :inject the follow-up message\n(get_follow_up_messages hook);
      elseif (the verify hook wants a revision?) then (yes)
        :emit `continuation`; inject the revision request\n(verify_answer hook, capped);
      else (GENUINELY DONE)
        :accept it as the FINAL answer\n(this is the only path that EXITS the loop normally);
      endif

    case ( ERROR or ABORTED )
      :end the run\n(error -> surface the exact message;  aborted -> stop);

    endswitch

  repeat while (keep going?) is (yes -> next step) not (no - done / error / max turns);
}

partition "6 . OUTPUT" #E0F2F1 {
  :stream every event -> all clients\n(thinking . text . tool activity . tool_progress . plan[PROPOSED]);
  :persist each message -> session JSONL (replayable next run);
}

:User sees the streamed answer;
stop

note right
  WHY A LOOP?  The LLM is STATELESS - it remembers nothing
  between calls. STEP 1 re-sends the FULL history every time;
  the model decides ONE next move; the loop runs it and feeds
  the result back. "Memory" = the loop re-feeding history.
  The loop ends only when the model returns a real answer with
  NO tool calls and NO continuation triggered (or error / max turns).
end note

note left
  THE `computer` TOOL IS A SEALED SUB-AGENT (not the main loop above).
  When the main agent calls it, an INNER loop runs on its own:
      screenshot primary monitor -> vision model picks ONE action
      -> open_browser / click / type / scroll / drag -> repeat
      (up to the step cap) -> return a TEXT SUMMARY.
  It is GUI-ONLY: it CANNOT call web_search / browser / read / etc.
  ==> So the main agent must give it a NARROW task, and do the
      faster public lookups (web_search / browser) at the MAIN level.
  This is exactly what PLAN-FIRST (gold) is meant to enforce:
  decompose -> `computer` for the logged-in step, fast tools for the rest.
end note

legend left
  | Colour | Meaning |
  | white | CURRENT logic (already in engine/native.py) |
  | gold | PROPOSED plan-first / `plan` tool - NOT built yet (under review) |
  | Loop exits when | final answer . error . aborted . max turns |
  | Continuation kinds | planning_only . reasoning_only . empty . revision . follow-up |
endlegend

@enduml
